{"seconds": 46.0, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! The main line is: **1...Qd5+ 2.Kh3 Rxd7 3.Rxd5 Rxd5**. Black wins material (rook vs pawn). This is clearly the best move - a devastating fork!\n\n**Best move:** Qd5+\n\n**Main line:** Qd5+ Kh3 Rxd7 Rxd5 Rxd5 cxd5\n\n**Motif:** fork\n\n**Explanation (80 words max):**\n\nYour queen on c5 can jump to d5, giving check and simultaneously attacking both white rooks on d1 and d7. White must move the king out of check\u2014there's no way to defend both rooks. After the king moves (say, Kh3), you simply capture the rook on d7 with Rxd7, winning a full rook. Even if White recaptures, you're up material. Watch for moves that attack two pieces at once, especially when they're undefended. A fork exploiting the king's limited escape squares wins material almost by force.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qd5+\", \"line\": [\"Qd5+\", \"Kh3\", \"Rxd7\", \"Rxd5\", \"Rxd5\", \"cxd5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "1r4k1/1n1Rr2p/4p1p1/2q1PpP1/2P2P1H/p1B5/P3Q1K1/3R4 b - - 1 41"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "1r4k1/1n1Rr2p/4p1p1/2q1PpP1/2P2P1P/p1B5/P3Q1K1/3R4 b - - 1 41"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "1r4k1/1n1Rr2p/4p1p1/2q1PpP1/2P2P1P/p1B5/P3Q1K1/3R4 b - - 1 41"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "1r4k1/1n1Rr2p/4p1p1/2q1PpP1/2P2P1P/p1B5/P3Q1K1/3R4 b - - 1 41"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1r4k1/1n1Rr2p/4p1p1/2q1PpP1/2P2P1P/p1B5/P3Q1K1/3R4 b - - 1 41", "move": "Qf2+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1r4k1/1n1Rr2p/4p1p1/2q1PpP1/2P2P1P/p1B5/P3Q1K1/3R4 b - - 1 41", "move": "Qg1+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1r4k1/1n1Rr2p/4p1p1/2q1PpP1/2P2P1P/p1B5/P3Q1K1/3R4 b - - 1 41", "move": "Qc6+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1r4k1/1n1Rr2p/4p1p1/2q1PpP1/2P2P1P/p1B5/P3Q1K1/3R4 b - - 1 41", "mo